+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** The five Section C design gaps leave loss states invisible in-game — the pool cap + map-wide shedding have no HUD surface, drop sites are never rendered, the lane bound has no depth readout, the SLA gauges never say *why* a packet dropped, and the strain rings don't say *what* is stuck. The user's surge-run confusion is evidence of this visibility debt (ruling 2026-08-14: "if players need a manual to play, that's a design failure").
+
+**Approach:** Add presentation-side HUD surfaces that read EXISTING per-tick data (the `Drop_Site` scratch + `Packet_Dropped` reason tags + `bundle_lane_count` + `len(packets)`), never re-derive or re-record: (1) a pool-pressure gauge, (2) drop-site markers at the shed bundle, (3) a per-lane queue-depth readout on the 5.8 QoS panel, (4) a pool/queue reason split on the SLA gauges, (5) a stuck-by-class line on the 5.2 node-health hover card. All surfaces are app-layer (drawn from `draw_hud`) — the harness T2 capture path never calls `draw_hud`, so goldens cannot shift.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Determinism spine: NO `LOG_VERSION` bump, no serialization changes, T1 byte-identical (prove with a green harness run). All new state is app-owned presentation state fed from per-tick sim data.
+- Golden discipline: T1 must not move; the surfaces are app-layer by construction (T2-invisible — the 5.2 card precedent); no re-bless, no silent drift.
+- Terminology canon (merged 2026-08-16, PR #55 — this branch rebased onto it): use **drop precedence** (never "drop ladder"), **congestion/utilization** (never "pressure/strain"), "lane" stays "lane" on the player HUD. New strings only; existing strings untouched. ASCII-only literals (lint gate 6).
+- Read-only over sim state; the draw never steps the sim (ODN-1). Integer-only display math.
+- All new surfaces honor quiet-at-green: no pixels when healthy (markers only when shedding; the reason split only when dropped > 0; the stuck line only when a node is actually stuck).
+- HUD anchors use the LIVE view dims (`v.win_w/win_h`), never the WIN_* constants (the font-resize precedent).
+
+**Ask First:** none — the briefing pre-approves the design direction ("your call, evidence-backed") and the step-02 spec checkpoint (standing orders override).
+
+**Never:** no balance/mechanic/canon-gameplay changes, no new command kinds, no serialization changes, no draw_world changes (that would be a T2 fold), no parallel strain surface (gap 5 extends the 5.2 card, never a duplicate), no `LOG_VERSION` bump.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Pool below 70% of cap | in-flight < 0.7×512, no E22 drops | gauge: green fill bar + count, no SHEDDING tag | N/A |
+| Pool at/over cap, E22 shedding | in-flight == 512, E22 sites in window | gauge: red + "SHEDDING +N" tag; NO map marker (E22 is map-wide) | N/A |
+| E9 shed at a bundle | drop_sites with bundle != NO_BUNDLE | marker at the bundle midpoint (red glyph + count), fading over the window | bundle demolished mid-window → skip (no screen pos) |
+| No drops | drop_sites empty | zero markers, no SHEDDING, reason split hidden | N/A |
+| SLA gauge with drops | acc.dropped > 0 | reason split appended: "pool N / queue M" | split only when dropped > 0 (0/0 hidden) |
+| Selected pipe on a bundle | sel_pipe → bundle slot | QoS panel queue-depth row: per-lane depth vs bound (lane_queue_packets) | pipe/bundle gone → panel already closes |
+| Node hover, stuck packets | node_stuck_by_class total > 0 | card gains "stuck: <class> N · <class> M" line | total == 0 → no extra line (card keeps 2 lines) |
+
