+## Design Notes
+
+**Why app-layer = zero golden risk (the spine proof).** The harness T2 capture path (`harness/goldens.odin:60-71`) calls only `draw_world` + `draw_forecast_panel` + `draw_health_meter` + `draw_crisis_banner` — never `draw_hud`. Every surface here is drawn from `draw_hud` (or by procs `draw_hud` calls), so T2 goldens cannot shift by construction; the green harness run is the proof. T1 is untouched because no core state or serialization changes; the only core addition is a pure read proc (`node_stuck_by_class`). App-owned presentation state (`drop_marks`, `drop_reasons`) is fed from `state.flow.drop_sites` after each `pp.step` — the same per-tick scratch the crisis engine reads — so it is derived, never recorded.
+
+**The pool gauge thresholds.** No dedicated pool thresholds exist in balance.json; the gauge reuses the `warnings` node amber/red pcts (70/90) so the whole telegraph speaks one vocabulary (the 5.2 coherence-by-choice precedent). The fill fraction is `len(f.packets) / pool_max_packets` — the exact in-flight measure the E22 guard uses (`flow_try_spawn` compares `len(f.packets) >= pool_max_packets`), so the gauge reads the sim's own truth.
+
+**Marker window + pause.** `drop_sites` is per-tick scratch (cleared each flow_step); the app accumulates a ~40-tick (2 s) ring for display. While paused (5.3), no steps run, so the ring freezes — markers persist for pause-and-plan, exactly the 5.3 canon.
+
+**Section B validation (numbers line up).** The gauge is diagnostic — Section B: the pool cap is fixed (512), a protection, not a lever; capacity levers (parallel pipes/tiers) show their effect as the bar recedes + SHEDDING stops. The reason split satisfies the pinned invariant (every drop is pool OR queue; demand_seen == delivered+dropped+live). The queue-depth row cites the 6-packet bound (`lane_queue_packets`) the E9 ladder sheds from.
